 "characters": 682,
 "text": "And this isn't a paper mission. The four main engines for Artemis Three reached Kennedy Space Center in July. The Orion capsule and its service module were joined in late July. On September thirtieth, technicians put the nose cones on the twin boosters, finishing the stack. More than two hundred and fifty parts from Artemis Two's Orion are being reused on later missions, and NASA says reused parts move some installation work up by about three months. Even the launch tower is being turned around for its next flight nearly fifty percent faster. And that missing upper stage? It isn't scrapped. NASA reassigned it to Artemis Four, the mission that actually has to reach the Moon.",
